  "source": "Independent hand audit of validation/m12/fixtures/cpp/*.{h,cpp} against C++ semantics and the M11 C++ contract (validated 1.000/1.000 in M11.10; symbols only). Symbols: namespaces -> namespace; classes/structs with bodies -> class; enum class -> enum with members -> enum_member; methods (declarations + out-of-line definitions incl. template methods Registry<T>::add) -> method; constructors -> constructor (normalized to the name \"constructor\"); members -> property; using aliases (`using Point = ...`) -> type; object-like macros with bodies -> constant. Noise (negative contract): include guards (#define NAME with no value body), forward declarations (`class X;` — no body: no symbol, no scope push), destructors (~Shape — compiler-managed), function-local variables, template parameters. File-scope static variables -> variable with private visibility (internal linkage). Relationships (family contract, matches Java M12.01 and C M12.16): contains = REAL container ownership only (namespace->class/enum/alias, class->method/property/constructor, enum->member) — never `global contains X`; calls = method -> callee (incl. member-function calls `obj.method()` whose field access is the call target — one edge per pair, never calls+uses for the same pair); uses = non-call field access only (never paired with references); references = include dependencies (global -> header) and type usage; extends = inheritance edge (Circle -> Shape); instantiates = new-expression allocations (none in fixtures). Cross-file declarations (e.g. Shape declared in Shape.h, used in Shape.cpp) do not resolve in a per-file parse — production wiring of the companion index is tracked by M12.44 (same note as Java/C).",
